        <detaileddescription>
<para>Construct specified floating-point value.</para><para>Creates a new floating-point constant AST node having the specified native value and type. See also, the constructor that takes a bit vector as its first argument, which is useful in cases where the native representation of a floating point value does not match the target machine&apos;s representation.</para><para>On the other hand, the default constructor creates a new floating-point value of unspecified type initialized to positive zero. We recommend using a constructor that takes a <ref refid="classSgAsmType" kindref="compound">SgAsmType</ref> argument instead. </para>        </detaileddescription>
